# Qwen3.5-0.8B on TT P150 AFTER W4 (#2107): eager decode perf-sampled, same method as the before log
# tree: row/BACKEND-TENSTORRENT-QWEN35 worktree head 0ac84a486 + the W4 bulk-staging change
#   (landed by the commit carrying this file); VLLM_CPP_TENSTORRENT=ON build, vllm-cli --device auto (default).
# single $HOME/gpu.lock hold, JIT-discard run first (0.173 tok/s, discarded), greedy 3-token leg, prompt 11 tok.
# perf record -F 199 -g -o /tmp/w4-perf.data -- build/examples/vllm-cli --model <Q35 snapshot 2fc0636471> \
#     --prompt "Write a short story about a robot learning to paint." --max-tokens 3
# leg: 16.961 s for 3 tokens = 0.177 tok/s (before-log same leg: 28.934 s = 0.104 tok/s -> +70%).
# Lock discipline: whole leg series under one flock hold on thalia (local non-fleet P150); no other board work interleaved.
#
# vs BEFORE (docs/bench-evidence/tt-qwen35-eager-profile-20260827.log):
#   vt::Tensor::Numel()                     27.09% -> 1.76%
#   EnsureDevice2D (flat)                   4.14%  -> below the 0.5% flat limit (absent from this flat section)
#   bfloat16::from_float                    2.62%  -> 1.09% (residual is download-side ToHostF32 / f32 masters)
#   transform_buffers<float,bfloat16>       2.63%  -> 0.97%
#   EnsureDevice2D->MatmulBTKernel chain    24.10% -> gone from the top callgraph
#   TT discovery (MetalContext::instance + DeviceManager::get_active_device + Cluster::get_chip
#     + get_closest_mmio_capable_chip)      14.52% -> 23.01% of a 41% smaller pie (~unchanged absolute seconds)
#   vt::cpu::Threadpool poll pair           11.39% -> 19.16% of the smaller pie
# Remaining wall attribution (next traceable hypothesis): per-upload tt-metal context/UMD/CQ work inside
#   from_span->to_device (buffer alloc + cluster queries + read_cq_host_ptr polling), i.e. the
#   tt-metal-internal half of W4 lever 2 that our file set cannot cache, plus CPU-threadpool spin.
